   "notes": "Describes the base Yi pretrained model (4K context), primary 6B. Block ops show the 6B head counts. Inheritance from LLaMA 2 rests on the statement that the code is based on LLaMA's implementation and that the listed changes are the modifications from LLaMA. RMSNorm, pre-norm, no biases, untied head and a sequential block are therefore marked inherited.\n\nThese were left not_stated:\n- d_ff: only the rule 8/3h is given, which is not an integer for h=4096.\n- head_dim.\n- norm eps.\n- RoPE pairing.\n- The adjusted RoPE ABF base, whose value is not given.\n\nExtensions are separate models, not the headline base architecture: 200K long context (continual pretraining only, no architecture change), Yi-VL (CLIP ViT-H/14 plus a 2-layer MLP projector) and Yi-9B depth upscaling (48 layers, made by duplicating layers 12-28 of the 6B model)."
  },
